{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1479468-blade-wolves-lodge-of-arms-2e-conversion","id":1479468,"title":"Blade Wolves (Lodge of Arms 2e conversion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-24T20:38:11-07:00","id":1479468,"title":"Blade Wolves (Lodge of Arms 2e conversion)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lodge of Arms</span></span></b></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Blade Wolves</i></span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pages 30-32 of Lodges the Faithful for lore</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bonds</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Lodge member applies half his Primal Urge, rounded up, as both a penalty against all attempts to disarm him and as a dice bonus to any rolls which involve the handling of weapons. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Aspiration:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Never refuse a direct challenge. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ban:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Can never yield what is yours.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sacred Hunt</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Lodge Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to assess his prey\u2019s combat skills. At a glance, he may determine his dots and Specialties in the following skills (Athletics, Brawl, Firearms, and Weaponry), as well as any Fighting Style Merits he has invested in. Furthermore, any weapons used against him do not apply dice tricks and lower their damage rating by the Uratha\u2019s Honorary Rank, to a minimum of 0L.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lodge Secrets</span></span></b><ul><li>The blade wolves believe that the hearts of humans store the resonance created from the actions they make, therefore, if they eat the heart of a great human warrior they will steal that resonance that is stored. They collect the hearts of their sacred hunts and devourer them in bloody rituals in order to harness their power.</li> <li>The fetish weapons of the blade wolves crave the blood of warriors, human or Uratha. This craving can be sated by drawing blood, not necessarily killing the warrior. This has led to a tradition of those who lose a duel between two blade wolves to allow the victor to draw blood from them, while the defeated party also offers blood to their own weapon. If a blade wolf ever finds himself alone with no worthy prey, they will offer their own blood to keep their weapon sated.</li> <li>Conflict drives the development of weapons and warriors, or so the blade wolves believe. In order to help speed up these developments, the adherents of the Lodge of Arms help to stir up conflict, although cold wars and arms races tend to the aim of their meddling when it comes to the development of new weapons, no one can deny the role war places in the crucible of the warriors.</li> <li>When a lodge member dies the other blade wolves attempt to recover their fetish weapon and store them away within faults deep in Hisil. It would be a sin to the weapon, its wielder, the lodge and their totem to allow someone else to wield the weapon in battle.</li> <li>It is not discouraged within the lodge to allow the spirit of your chosen weapon to claim you, at least for a time, in order to strengthen the bond between weapon and warrior.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tools</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Lodge of arms has access to the Lodge Stronghold merit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rite of the Duel (Wolf Rite \u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dueling with other members of the Lodge of Arms is one of the great pleasures of lodge membership for many werewolves. With the level of skill many lodge members possess, and the frightening power of their weapons, the lodge needed to find a way to prevent members from killing each other too frequently. This rite was the response. It creates an area in which the spirits of weapons are suppressed, rendering them much less effective in killing opponents. This rite is always performed before any duel between lodge members.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When performing this rite the rite master must mark an area to be designated for the effect to take effect.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Symbols:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Blood, Dueling, Weapons </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sample Rite:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rite master sets a fire burning in the center of the dueling circle, and then walks around the boundaries of the area, marking it out with a weapon, stick or even his hands. Once the circle is complete, the rite master must douse the fire, thereby symbolically quenching the passion of spirits within the circle. At the end of the rite, he growls in the manner of a patient parent and invites the combatants into the ring. (Presence + Occult)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extended (15 successes; each roll represents 1 minute)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The rite blesses the area designated by the rite master. While within the marked circle, any lethal damage received from weapons is downgraded to bashing damage. This rite cannot affect attacks made with natural weapons, and its effects are lost if a character leaves the circle. If the markings that designated the area are physically broken the rite\u2019s effects end, otherwise the area remains empowered for the duration of the scene.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forging Arms (Wolf Rite \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the central rite of the Lodge of Arms, a rite which bonds a spirit to a weapon and both to the lodge member who will carry the weapon for the rest of his life. The rite only takes place after days of preparation. Once all the elements are in place, the weapon built, a spirit captured and bound and the werewolf\u2019s own spiritual aspect exhausted by days of endurance, the rite can begin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Symbols:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Binding, Forging, Strength, Weapons, The Spirit\u2019s Influence(s)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sample Rite:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Under the command of the rite master, the new initiate carries out repeated sets of practiced forms with the weapon. They can be anything from a series of guards, parries and attacks with a blade to different firing positions and target shots with a gun. As the new weapon-holder works, the lodge members who built the weapon and helped trap the spirits chant the words of the ritual with increasing volume and speed. The new initiate is expected to match these changes by increasing the speed and intensity of his exercises. This continues until the initiate is at the very point of exhaustion. Then, just before the young werewolf collapses, the rite master speaks the words of binding in First Tongue. (Dexterity + Expression)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 essence for each extended action roll from the rite master, and an additional 1 essence from each participant at the rites conclusion.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extended (30 successes: each roll represents 30 minutes)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spirits of the werewolf, the forged weapon, and the bound spirit. momentarily fuse, infusing each other with new strength. The initiate is now a member of the lodge and is bound to their weapon, which they gain a +3 to all actions with, while also gaining any benefits from the bound spirit as per the fetish rules. (WtF 146-147)</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-15-2023, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T20:40:46-07:00","id":1479469,"title":"","content":"Hey all, a player in my WtF game wanted to join this lodge and I couldn't find a 2e conversion that I was happy with, so I took a lot from the book it originally appeared it, took things I liked from the conversions I had seen, and filled in the rest. Thought I'd share it for feed back and so others can use it, as is or for inspiration!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T00:15:16-07:00","id":1479475,"title":"","content":"By Dexterity + Performance in the second rite, I assume you meant Dexterity + Expression ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T09:45:37-07:00","id":1479488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1479468-blade-wolves-lodge-of-arms-2e-conversion?p=1479475#post1479475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By Dexterity + Performance in the second rite, I assume you meant Dexterity + Expression ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, good catch. It was Dexterity + Performance in 1e and I copied that over as the example rite and missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}